        "content": "# Unitman SLOs and baseline (2026-11-18)\n\nSource: `plans/memory-baseline/report.md`. Local stand = dev image with Xdebug/xhprof, so absolute numbers are higher than production.\n\n## Latency SLOs (k6 thresholds in `tests/load/k6`)\n\n| Scenario | SLO p95 | Baseline median p95 |\n|----------|---------|---------------------|\n| `POST /api/unit/list` (`{\"limit\":100,\"offset\":0}`) | <= 200 ms | 72 ms |\n| `POST /api/unit/moi` (`{\"limit\":10,\"offset\":0}`) | <= 200 ms | 132 ms |\n| `saveSteps`, 10 steps | <= 120 ms | 43 ms |\n| `saveSteps`, 500 steps | <= 150 ms | 50 ms |\n| `saveSteps`, 400 x 6 KB (~2.4 MiB) | <= 350 ms | 219 ms |\n| Upload 1 MiB | <= 200 ms | avg 84 ms, max 111 ms |\n| Upload 50 MiB | <= 5 s | 2.76-3.06 s |\n| Upload 199 MiB | <= 20 s | 12.04 s |\n\n## Memory baseline\n\n| Metric | Baseline | SLO |\n|--------|----------|-----|\n| Idle PSS | 1938-1952 MB | <= 2.0 GB |\n| PSS after load | 2314-2417 MB | <= 2.6 GB |\n| Peak HTTP worker RSS | 97.3 MB (limit `max_worker_memory: 100`) | 0 worker restarts |\n| `rr serve` after 199 MiB upload | ~310 MB, not returned after pause | watch |\n| Worker pools | HTTP 12, Jobs 20, Temporal 13, background services 24 | - |\n\nNotes:\n- This RoadRunner version (3.0.0) does not export `rr_jobs_jobs_num`; Jobs queue activity is visible via `rr_jobs_jobs_ok`, `rr_jobs_jobs_err`, `rr_jobs_jobs_requeue`, and worker counts via `rr_jobs_total_workers` / `rr_jobs_workers_*`.\n- `max_worker_memory` is a soft limit: restarts are visible as drops in `rr_http_worker_memory_bytes` and changes in `rr_http_worker_state`.\n- Load scripts: `tests/load/k6/*.js`; large uploads: `tests/load/upload-large.sh`.\n",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "SLO thresholds and baseline",
      "type": "text"
    }
